The grey wolf ends its hunt by attacking its prey when the prey stops their movement. The mathematical model indicates the approach to the prey by reducing the value of a. A variation is likewise diminished by ấ with A being randomly chosen from the interval [-2a, 2a], where the value decreases from 2 to 0 throughout the iterations. The GWO algorithm enables its search agents to adjust their positions according to the alpha, beta, and delta locations and attack the prey as shown in Eq. (18).
